      "message": "[From Jetski review] Soundness / encapsulation concern:\n\n1. Because `BigEnoughBuffer.0`, `BigEnoughBuffer::write_slice`, `StringOutputBuffer::reserve`, and `Writable` are all safe and `pub`, safe code can trigger UB (out-of-bounds write) without writing `unsafe` — e.g. by calling `buffer.reserve(0).write_slice(b\"overflow\")` or implementing `Writable` with a `maximum_size()` smaller than what `write_to_buf()` writes.\n2. Per `AGENTS.md` (\"Data members should not be public without good reason\" / \"Keep modules, structs, and fields private or `pub(crate)` by default\"), could we make the tuple field `pub(crate) \u0026\u0027a mut *mut u8`, and make either `Writable` an `unsafe trait` + `reserve` / `write_slice` `unsafe fn` (or keep `reserve` / `BigEnoughBuffer` internal to `append` / `buf_write!`)?",
