      "side": 1,
      "message": "[From Jetski review] Bug: In Rust, `char` is a 4-byte Unicode scalar value (1–4 bytes in UTF-8), not a single byte. Casting `*self as u8` silently truncates non-ASCII characters into invalid UTF-8 bytes, which will then cause `StringOutputBufferToString` (`rust::String(buffer.str())`) to throw `std::invalid_argument` across the `noexcept` FFI boundary and abort.\n\nUsing `self.len_utf8()` and `encode_utf8`:\n```rust\nimpl Writable for char {\n    fn maximum_size(\u0026self) -\u003e usize {\n        self.len_utf8()\n    }\n\n    fn write_to_buf(\u0026self, buf: \u0026mut BigEnoughBuffer\u003c\u0027_\u003e) {\n        let mut tmp \u003d [0u8; 4];\n        buf.write_slice(self.encode_utf8(\u0026mut tmp).as_bytes());\n    }\n}\n```\nwill constant-fold to a 1-byte write for ASCII literals like `\u0027\\n\u0027` while handling non-ASCII `char`s safely (and also lets us remove `BigEnoughBuffer::write\u003cT: Copy\u003e`).",
      "isAi": true,
